--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -7,29 +7,46 @@ Every person registers and logs in, and sees only **their own** devices.
 - **Backend:** Node.js REST API (`server/`), built-in `http` and `node:sqlite`, no npm packages needed
 - **Database:** SQLite file created automatically at `server/data.db`
 
+## How the network is organized
+Your network is arranged the way a real one is: **Department > Router > Ethernet port > IP address / prefix**.
+
+1. **Add a department** (for example Accounting) with the big **Add department** button.
+2. Click the department, then **Add router** (for example R1).
+3. Click the router, then **Add IP address**. Pick the **Department** and **Router** from the drop-down boxes (every department and router you added appears there automatically), type the **Ethernet port** (for example Gi0/0), the **IP address** and its **prefix** (for example 24), and the device that uses it.
+
+Everything is shown as big, clickable buttons:
+
+![Departments](docs/departments.png)
+
+Click a department to see its routers:
+
+![Routers](docs/routers.png)
+
+Click a router to see its Ethernet ports, each with its IP addresses and prefixes (for example `192.168.20.1/24`):
+
+![Ethernet ports](docs/ethernet-ports.png)
+
+Add IP address form (the Department and Router boxes fill themselves from what you added):
+
+![Add IP address](docs/add-ip-address.png)
+
 ## Interface
 
 ![Dashboard](docs/dashboard.png)
 
 A dark "CRM style" dashboard with a button sidebar, gradient cards and charts.
 
-- **Sidebar buttons:** your profile, **Overview** (Dashboard, Subnet map, Devices), **Device types** and **Assignment** filter buttons with live counts, and a **Download report** card that exports every device to CSV.
-- **Gradient summary cards:** total devices (and how many were added this week), subnet usage with a progress bar, Static / DHCP counts, and the next free address (click it to assign it).
-- **Charts** (drawn in plain SVG, no extra packages): **Devices over time** (last 14 days, hover for numbers), **Devices by type**, **Static vs DHCP**, and **Address usage by block** of the current subnet.
-- **Quick actions:** Add device, Use next free IP, View subnet map, Export all devices.
-- **Filters:** click a type or assignment in the sidebar and the device list filters at once. Remove a filter with its chip.
-- **Subnet map** and a searchable, sortable **device list** (press **/** to search).
-- **Light and dark mode** (dark is the default, the moon/sun button switches) and a **phone layout** with a slide-in menu.
+- **Network card:** the big-button Department > Router > Ethernet port navigation above. You can rename or delete a department or router (deleting also deletes what is inside it, after a confirmation).
+- **Sidebar buttons:** your profile, **Overview** (Dashboard, Network, Subnet map), your **Departments** with their IP counts, **Device types** and **Assignment** filter buttons, and a **Download report** card that exports every IP address to CSV.
+- **Gradient summary cards:** total IP addresses (and how many were added this week), subnet usage with a progress bar, number of departments and routers, and the next free address (click it to assign it).
+- **Charts** (plain SVG, no extra packages): **IP addresses over time** (last 14 days, hover for numbers), **Devices by type**, **Static vs DHCP**, and **Address usage by block** of the current subnet.
+- **Search and filters:** type in the search box, or click a type or assignment in the sidebar, and the big buttons are replaced by a table of matching IP addresses showing the full path (department, router, port). Remove a filter with its chip.
+- **Quick actions:** Add IP address, Add department, Use next free IP, View subnet map, Export all.
+- **Subnet map** of used and free addresses, **light and dark mode**, and a **phone layout** with a slide-in menu.
 
