 ## Requirements
 Node.js **22.13 or newer** (`node -v` to check). Node 22 prints an "experimental" warning for SQLite. That is normal.
@@ -55,6 +72,9 @@ Open http://localhost:5173.
 
 **Upgrading from the version without accounts:** the old `server/data.db` has no owner for its devices, so the server discards the old device table on first start. If you see any database error, stop the server and delete `server/data.db`, then start again.
 
+## Upgrading from the version without departments
+IP addresses saved earlier have no router yet, so the server moves them into a department and router both called **Unassigned** (with the port "Not set" and prefix 24). Open them there and edit each one to put it in the right place.
+
 ## Run the tests
 
     cd server
@@ -68,10 +88,15 @@ Open http://localhost:5173.
 | POST | /api/login | Log in (sets a cookie) |
 | POST | /api/logout | Log out (clears the cookie) |
 | GET | /api/me | Who is logged in (401 if nobody) |
-| GET | /api/devices | List **your** devices, sorted by IP |
-| POST | /api/devices | Add a device (409 if the IP is taken, with a free suggestion) |
-| PUT | /api/devices/:id | Update a device |
-| DELETE | /api/devices/:id | Delete a device |
+| GET | /api/departments | Your departments, with router and IP counts |
+| POST | /api/departments | Add a department (409 if the name exists) |
+| PUT / DELETE | /api/departments/:id | Rename / delete (deletes its routers and IP addresses too) |
+| GET | /api/routers | Your routers, with their department, Ethernet port and IP counts |
+| POST | /api/routers | Add a router to a department (409 if the department already has that name) |
+| PUT / DELETE | /api/routers/:id | Rename / delete (deletes its IP addresses too) |
+| GET | /api/devices | Your IP addresses with `cidr`, `ether`, `routerName` and `departmentName`, sorted by IP |
+| POST | /api/devices | Add one: `routerId`, `ether`, `ip`, `prefix`, `name`, `type`, `status`, `notes` (409 if the IP is taken, with a free suggestion) |
+| PUT / DELETE | /api/devices/:id | Update / delete an IP address |
 | GET | /api/subnet?cidr=192.168.1.0/24 | Used and free addresses for a subnet (up to /22) |
 | GET | /api/types | Allowed device types |
 
